### A box contains 27 marbles some are blue and others are green. If a marble is drawn at random from the box, the probability that it is blue is 1 / 3. How many green marbles are there in the box?

Solution - Given that,

 total Marbles = 27
 P(b) = 1/3
 Green marbles =?

 P(b) = blue / total
 1/3 = blue / 27
 blue = 9
 then , Answer - (green = 18) 
